    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n84247" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ποι-ητέος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">α</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>to be made</i> or <i>done,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				1.191
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				7.15
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Art.</u>
				27
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>R.</u>
				361c
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐλάβειά τινος π.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Antipho
					3.3.11
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ π.,</span>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τί δεῖ ποιεῖν</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				4.99
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ποιητέον,</span>
			<i>one must make</i> or <i>do,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				And.
				3.16
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Onos.
				22.2
			</span></i>, etc.:—from 
				Med.
			, <i>one must deem,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">περὶ πολλοῦ π. τὸ ἑαυτὸν γιγνώσκειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>Mem.</u>
					4.2.30
				</span></i>
			.</div>
